# ============================================================
# AIDLC EXECUTION RULES — Fish Farm Management System (FMS) — surface: backend
# ============================================================
## Source of truth
The specs in ../fish-farm-context-files/ are the source of truth. This repo holds only code
generated from them. Never hand-edit code to fix a problem — fix the spec, then regenerate.
The coding constitution is ../fish-farm-context-files/CLAUDE.md; when it and a prompt conflict,
CLAUDE.md wins unless the human overrides in chat.

## Where things live
- Specs/plans/contracts: ../fish-farm-context-files/  (start at ../fish-farm-context-files/INDEX.md)
- The API contract: ../fish-farm-context-files/contracts/openapi.yaml
- This repo: generated NestJS backend code only (modular monolith, Clean Architecture)
- Shared packages are hosted here under `packages/{calendar,shared}` and published to web/mobile (OI-1)

## Non-negotiable invariants (from CLAUDE.md §2 — never violate)
- Tenant isolation: every project-owned query is filtered by project_id via the project-scope
  guard + scoped-repository base. No endpoint queries project data unscoped. Non-member → 403/404
  uniformly (never leak another project's existence). A negative isolation test is a deliverable.
- Domain purity: the domain layer imports zero frameworks (no NestJS/TypeORM/HTTP). Dependencies
  point inward only.
- TypeORM Data Mapper in infrastructure only; never @Entity/@Column on a domain class; never
  Active Record. synchronize:false always; every schema change ships a reversible migration.
- No secrets in code (env only). Money as integer minor units / decimal, never float. UUID v4.
- Bangla dates only via packages/calendar — never Intl/ICU.

## Per-task workflow (never skip)
1. READ the task card in ../fish-farm-context-files/BACKLOG.md (cards tagged surface=backend) + its module file
2. ASSEMBLE context: parent IDs, glossary terms, relevant ADRs, the contract, current code
3. GENERATE code AND tests (one test per AC) — the backend IMPLEMENTS contracts/openapi.yaml
4. VERIFY: tests pass, coverage met, lint/type/security clean, contract tests pass, build succeeds
5. REVIEW: a human checks intent/correctness (not syntax)
6. If wrong → fix the SPEC or card, regenerate. Do NOT hand-patch.
7. INTEGRATE: merge; update ../fish-farm-context-files/TRACEABILITY_MATRIX.md + MODULE_PROGRESS_TRACKER.md
8. COMMIT with TASK- and MOD- IDs. One unit per session; never bundle units.

## Guardrails — STOP and ask a human, never decide alone:
- Changing a frozen ADR, or changing contracts/openapi.yaml (it affects other surfaces)
- Adding/removing a data entity or shared schema; defining a reserved CON-049…055 endpoint
- Anything touching auth, payments/finance, PII, or compliance
- Contradicting an NFR threshold; adding an unapproved dependency
- Any scope beyond the card's acceptance criteria
- Unresolved Open Items (OI-1…OI-6) that a card depends on

## Never: write specs into this repo; implement without reading the card; mark done without
passing ACs; rename an ID/file without updating every cross-reference, the contract, the matrix, INDEX.md
# ============================================================
